<title>USA: INTERVIEW - Monterey Pasta Q3 an aberration.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - Monterey Pasta Q3 an aberration.</headline>
<byline>Barbara Grady</byline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monterey Pasta Co chief executive Ned Dean described the gourmet pasta company's current slowdown as &quot;a hiccup&quot; on its way to profitability.</p>
<p>&quot;It looks like a three or four month push in terms of our time scale,&quot; Dean told Reuters of what is needed to get profitable. However, he did not commit to fourth quarter profitability.</p>
<p>Monterey's stock fell nearly two points midday losing more than a third of its value and closed down 1-1/8 at 4-1/2 after it warned it would have continued losses in the third quarter.</p>
</text>
